Bad Kissinger chess club has a prominent member
The chess club "Chess Friends Bad Kissingen", which was founded three months ago, has included another member in its ranks, thus increased the number of members to 19 players.
The new member is the entrepreneur Paul Gauselmann, a passionate chess and tennis player who stayed more than 40 times in Bad Kissingen for the cure.
Gauselmann is the bearer of the Federal Cross of Merit 1st class and an honorary citizen of the cities Espelkamp and Lübbecke.
Gauselmann supported the chess club in Bad Kissingen with a donation, which Chairman Alfred Klein accepted.
This makes it possible to include chess players who are unable to pay the membership fee.
Youth work and finding talent should also be promoted.
Gauselmann hopes that membership in the chess club and also friendly contact to the tennis club "Rot-Weiß" will be seen as an expression of his connection with the spa town.
Quartier's office seeks direct contact
Saludis and the Antonisticton’s Old People’s Centre have teamed up under the cloak of the Social Foundation and opened a new point of contact at Graf-Stauffenberg-Platz.
In addition to consultations, you can also participate in courses there.
The Social Foundation pulls it down from the mountain to the city center.
More precisely to Graf-Stauffenberg-Platz.
A new district office was recently opened there.
Here, right next to the shopping market, seniors and advice seekers will now receive information on questions such as long-term care insurance or health and long-term care insurance.
For years, we have found with our outpatient nursing service that nursing relatives are often left alone.
There are an infinite number of questions.
"It is not uncommonly that many services of the coffers are not used, because the complexity of the insurances is hardly understood," explained the new landlord Jutta Weigand, who is also responsible as a business unit manager for the Antonistift and the Bürgerspital as well as for the outpatient service "Amadeus".
In addition to the consultations, the new district office also offers prevention, health courses and wellness.
For this purpose, the Saludis was taken on board.
Therefore, one can take advantage of additional offers such as fall prevention, memory training or physiotherapeutic treatment.
The offers of the senior center and the Saludis complement each other in an ideal way.
Saludis stands for prevention, prevention and rehab.
"The senior center for care and care," described Heike Riedel, managing director of Saludis.
The reason for the opening of the new district office in the city center, both managing directors see in particular in demographic change.
Because this makes a good decentralized infrastructure in the individual districts of Bamberg essential in the future.
In addition, underlined Mayor Wolfgang Metzner (SPD) at the inauguration celebrations, the district office is also devoting itself to isolation in old age: "There are numerous events and offers on the program and they invite you to a regular convivial get-together".
In this way, the Social Foundation makes a great contribution that seniors can live as independently as possible and well in their familiar environment.
The district office is open Monday, Wednesday and Friday from 9 a.m. to 2 p.m., Tuesday and Thursday from 4 p.m. to 6 p.m. and on Saturday from 10 a.m. to 12 p.m.
Eintracht Bamberg v Würzburger Kickers on October 6
Now it is official: After the date for the match FC Eintracht Bamberg against the third-division Würzburger Kickers had not yet been determined due to renovation work on the Fuchsparkstadion, October 6 has now been set as the date.
FC Eintracht Bamberg's encounter in the quarter-finals of the Bavarian Football Totopokal against the third division FC Würzburger Kickers has now been definitively terminated.
It will be played on Tuesday, October 6, at 7 p.m. at Bamberg’s Fuchsparkstadion.
"We are glad that we now know when the game takes place, now we have planning certainty," said FCE team manager Karlheinz Hümmer, who also points to the ticket pre-sales that have now started.
It's special for our team to play against a third division team.
We are therefore hoping for numerous spectators, and not without reason, because floodlight games have a special charm.
FC Eintracht Bamberg moved into the round of the last 16 teams in 2010 by victories at the Bezirksligisten 1. FC Oberhaid (3:1) and at home against the regional league club 1. FC Schweinfurt 05 (3:2).
The winner of the competition will receive 5000 euros and qualifies for the first round of the DFB Club Cup 2016/2017.
Defending champion is third-leaguer SpVgg Unterhaching.
Viennese architect Karl Mang has died aged 92
Karl Mang, one of the doyens of Viennese architecture, has died.
He died on September 5 at the age of 92, as the Künstlerhaus announced on Tuesday.
With Mang, the Künstlerhaus lost an honorary member and at the same time "one of the most important architects of the second half of the 20th century in Vienna," as it said in the broadcast.
Born 1922 in Vienna, Mang studied architecture at the Technical University in Vienna with Friedrich Lehmann during and after the Second World War.
Since 1952 he worked as a freelance architect, but also worked as a teacher, writer and head of the institute.
From 1972 to 1983 he was president of the Austrian Institute of Design.
In the 1980s, he was commissioned with the furnishing of the treasurial chamber in Vienna’s Hofburg and the conversion of Palais Lobkowitz into the Austrian Theatre Museum.
