"We were very happy about that," Stadler said.
The stranded train passengers had switched from an ICE to a regional train towards Passau on Sunday evening in Wels, in order after the short-term proclamation that the rail traffic to Germany was stopped, but still across the border.
However, the regional train was parked in front of the border in Wernstein am Inn.
In Wernstein, cross-borders is generally very popular.
The bridge festivation connected with the Bavarian neighbors on Sunday sociably, the day before a two-bridge run sporty - organized by the Union Wernstein and Bavaria from Neukirchen.
The fact that Viktor Orbán is now sending tens of thousands more to us is a logical result of a hypocritical policy:
Instead of immediately helping in the Röszke camp with the establishment of structures that ensure humanity, our chancellor has placed the attitude of the Hungarian government into the haze of National Socialism.
The victims of this policy are not only those Austrians, who are now confronted with chaotic conditions in the border areas.
Refugees, too, will have to find that the "promised land" she has invited and welcomed is nothing but another refugee camp.
It will be a great challenge, in view of the continuing flow of refugees and the approaching winter, to create decent conditions for those seeking protection.
And it will be an even bigger one - to maintain peace, security and stability in Austria.
Konrad looking for 35,000 winter-proof quarters
Konrad has his hands full with refugee accommodation.
Christian Konrad is used to make sure his word carries weight.
