However, the right-hander stabbed Sano on three pitches for his fifth save.
At the start of the game, Detroit benefited from an as-yet immovable Phil Hughes.
The Tigers scored three runs in the first-two innings against the right-hander veteran, who had been dropped from the injured list before the game after missing more than a month because of a back injury.
